BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260814T134500Z
DTEND:20260814T143000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T000000Z
SUMMARY:Book Babies
DESCRIPTION:Please join us on Fridays at 9:45 a.m. for special bonding time 
 with your little one (ages 0-24 months)! At this lapsit-style storytime\, 
 we will spend about 20 minutes engaging in structured learning through 
 bounces\, rhymes\, songs\, and books\, followed by 15-45 minutes of 
 unstructured play and socialization time.\n\nNote: A television is used 
 during the first part of the program to display the words to the songs and 
 rhymes (to support adult engagement)\; there are no moving pictures. \n\nTo 
 celebrate 2026 Summer Reading and its theme\, "Unearth a Story\," we will 
 be focusing on dinosaurs from June 12 - August 14\, 2026.\n\nAll are 
 welcome! If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact Chelsea at cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible!
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-17225733
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17225733
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260814T140000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T000000Z
SUMMARY:Memory Cafe
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a monthly activity for people with dementia 
 and their caregivers. Memory Cafes host activities designed to engage in 
 the present\, without the expectations of using short-term memory or 
 forward thinking. This month\, we will celebrate summer reading by making 
 dinosaur zen gardens! \n\nThis program will be held on Aug 14\, 2026\, at 
 10 a.m. at the North Regional Library in the Small Program Room. The 
 address is 221 Milton Rd.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or 
 accommodation needs\, please contact me at dpeterson@dconc.gov. We ask that 
 all requests be made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to 
 ensure we can provide the best accommodations possible! Please email me if 
 you plan to attend and have nut allergies so that we can make 
 accommodations.
LOCATION:North Regional - Children's Programming Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Desiree Peterson":MAILTO:dpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Low Sensory Stimulation, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-17206680
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17206680
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260814T143000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T000000Z
SUMMARY:"Unearth a Story" Bilingual Storytime with Ms. Melanie!
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Bilingual Storytime at the Bragtown Branch Library! 
 This engaging and interactive program is perfect for children and families 
 looking to enjoy stories\, songs\, and activities in both English and 
 Spanish.\n\nWhether you're fluent in both languages or just starting out\, 
 everyone is welcome to share in the fun and learning. Bilingual Storytime 
 is a wonderful way to build language skills\, make new friends\, and 
 celebrate our vibrant community.
LOCATION:Bragtown Branch Library (3200 Dearborn Dr)
ORGANIZER;CN="Melanie Jimenez":MAILTO:mrjimenez@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Bilingual, Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16497371
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16497371
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260814T143000Z
DTEND:20260814T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T000000Z
SUMMARY:Preschool Storytime
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Fridays for Preschool Storytime! Designed for 
 children ages 3–5\, this interactive storytime includes books\, songs\, 
 movement\, and a simple craft or coloring activity\, though children of all 
 ages are welcome to attend. Registration is encouraged to help us prepare 
 enough craft materials.\n\nPreschool Storytime will be led by Children’s 
 Librarians Tina and Miles. See below for the schedule of 
 presenters:\n\n\n	Friday\, June 5 – Tina\n	Friday\, June 12 – 
 Tina\n	Friday\, June 26 – Miles\n	Friday\, July 10 – Miles\n	Friday\, 
 July 17 – Tina\n	Friday\, July 24 – Miles\n	Friday\, July 31 – 
 Tina\n	Friday\, August 7 – Tina\n	Friday\, August 14 – Miles\n	Friday\, 
 August 21 – Tina\n	Friday\, August 28 – Miles\n\n
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time, Summer Reading
UID:LibCal-14288-16866844
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16866844
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260814T143000Z
DTEND:20260814T153000Z
DTSTAMP:20260814T000000Z
SUMMARY:Scented Storytime! @ South Regional Library
DESCRIPTION:Join us for storytime and scented activities with Bright Black 
 Candle Co! Through reading\, singing\, and crafts we'll discover the 
 connection of storytelling and scent. All pre-school aged children are 
 welcome! Please register to secure your spot and help us make we have 
 enough materials for everyone.\n\nView all Scented Storytimes here: Scented 
 Storytime – Durham County Library
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ciera Williams":MAILTO:cbwilliams@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Library Fest, Story Time
