SUMMARY:GM 101 Volunteer Players (morning)
DESCRIPTION:We are looking for experienced Dungeons & Dragons players 
 willing to assist in our GM 101 program series! As part of the course\, 
 participants will practice GMing the first session of their campaigns. We 
 need experienced D&D players to participate in these playtests and offer 
 gentle\, constructive feedback to the GM. There will be experienced GMs 
 there to observe and answer questions\, so your only job will be to play 
 and offer feedback. \n\nHalf of the GMs will run their playtest sessions 
 August 15\, 10 a.m. - 1 p.m. and the other half will run theirs 2 - 5 p.m. 
 Please sign up for one or both sessions and help us nurture these new 
 GMs!\n\nWe will be meeting in the front meeting room at South Regional 
 Library. The sessions will begin promptly at 10 a.m. and 2 p.m.\, so please 
 make sure you're on time! Volunteer players who arrive late may not be able 
 to join a game that's already in progress.
