BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260822T173000Z
DTEND:20260822T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260822T000000Z
SUMMARY:Nic Cage Acting Workshop
DESCRIPTION:"How does he do it?" \n\nThat's a question myself and many 
 others ask themselves while watching a Nicolas Cage performance. How can 
 one man contain so much range and is able to go from 0 to 100 in the blink 
 of an eye? Well now we can finally start to answer these big questions. 
 Join us on the 2nd floor programming room for an acting workshop dedicated 
 to studying the craft of the Cage. From his Oscar nominated turns\, to 
 voiceover roles\, the memes and everything in between\, this is a wholly 
 sincere program where we will learn and practice techniques that the legend 
 himself has utilized.\n\nThis workshop will consist of acting warmup 
 exercises\, improv and some light scene work. Be ready to be on your feet 
 and do some silly things! Everyone is welcome and it's all in the name of 
 the Cage (and good fun)!
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Miles Simpson-Quigley":MAILTO:msquigley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17197544
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17197544
