BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260822T190000Z
DTEND:20260822T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260822T000000Z
SUMMARY:The Declaration of Independence is coming to the library....And Nic Cage is going to steal it!
DESCRIPTION:The Declaration of Independence is coming to the library....And 
 Nic Cage is going to steal it! \n\nCelebrate two of America’s national 
 treasures: The Declaration of Independence and Nicolas Cage at Main 
 Library! \n\n \n\nStart the celebration at 1:30 pm and learn How Does He Do 
 It? A Nic Cage Acting Workshop a question myself and many others ask 
 themselves while watching a Nicolas Cage performance. How can one man 
 contain so much range and is able to go from 0 to 100 in the blink of an 
 eye? Well now we can finally start to answer these big questions. This 
 acting workshop is dedicated to studying the craft of the Cage. From his 
 Oscar nominated turns\, to voiceover roles\, the memes and everything in 
 between\, this is a wholly sincere program where we will learn and practice 
 techniques that the legend himself has utilized. \n\nThis workshop will 
 consist of acting warmup exercises\, improv and some light scene work. Be 
 ready to be on your feet and do some silly things! Everyone is welcome and 
 it's all in the name of the Cage (and good fun)! \n\nThis program is for 
 all ages and starts on Saturday August 22nd at 1:30 p.m. in the 
 Children’s Programming Room located on the second floor of the Main 
 Library.  Register for How Does He Do It? A Nic Cage Acting Workshop !\n\n 
 \n\n\n\nWant to prepare yourself for the Declaration of Independence coming 
 to Main Library? Sneak your way into the Main Library auditorium for a 
 special film screening of National Treasure and learn how to steal it!  
 \n\nActivity sheets will be available! A limited amount of free DVD’s of 
 National Treasure and National Treasure: Book of Secrets will be available 
 thanks to generous donations from the community to The Friends of the 
 Durham Library !\n\nReleased in 2004 Nic Cage plays Benjamin Franklin 
 Gates\, a historian\, along with a computer expert and archivist\, search 
 for a massive lost Freemason treasure\, which includes a map hidden on the 
 back of the United States Declaration of Independence.  \n\nSaturday August 
 22nd starting at 3 pm in the Main Library auditorium this film runs about 2 
 ½ hours and is rated PG. \n\nRegister on this page for the film screening 
 to receive a program reminder! \n\n \n\nStill not enough Nic Cage for you? 
 Complete the National Treasure scavenger hunt in the Children’s area and 
 win a prize from the treasure box! \n\nThe scavenger hunt is suitable for 
 juveniles accompanied by an adult and is an all day drop in event.  \n\n 
 \n\nOn display will be an original American Library Association READ poster 
 featuring Nic Cage! \n\n \n\nParking is available in the library parking 
 lot or at the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street 
 which is behind the apartments directly across the street from the 
 library.\n\n \n\nThere will be no live Nic Cage's at the event.\n\n 
 \n\nQuestions? Email Megan at mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, High Sensory Stimulation, Movie, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-16561982
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16561982
END:VEVENT
