SUMMARY:3D Printing Orientation Part 1 (virtual)
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to 3D print from idea to design to fabrication! In 
 this two part orientation series\, you will learn how to design and 3D 
 print your own ideas.\n\nNote: You must sign up and attend both orientation 
 parts to gain 3D printer access. If you have take one (but not both) of the 
 orientations\, you can register for this set and only attend the 
 orientation part you are missing.\n\nIf you are under the age of 13 you 
 must have a parent or guardian present to sign up for 3D Printer OS to send 
 prints to the library.\n\n \n\n3D Printing Orientation Part 1: 3D Design - 
 Wednesday\, September 2nd\, 4-5pm\n\n\n	Learn about the basics of 3D 
 printing and how to create your own design.\n\n\n3D Printing Orientation 
 Part 2: Printing Designs - Wednesday\,  September 9th\, 4-5pm\n\n\n	Learn 
 about our specific 3D printers and the software you use to send a 
 print.\n\n\n \n\nRegistration required. Sessions are held virtually over 
 Zoom.
