SUMMARY:Mental Health First Aid
DESCRIPTION:Join Durham County Public Health for Mental Health First Aid\, 
 a one-day course that teaches you how to identify\, understand and respond 
 to signs of mental health and substance use challenges among adults. It 
 will cover topics such as:\n\n Common signs and symptoms of mental health 
 challenges.\n Common signs and symptoms of substance use challenges.\n How 
 to interact with a person in crisis.\n How to connect a person with help.\n 
 Expanded content on trauma\, substance use and self-care.\n\nThe course is 
 open to adults who wish to learn how to respond with the Mental Health 
 First Aid Action Plan. \n\nRegistration is Required and closes September 
 6th. \n\nAttending this course earns you an extra entry into the One Walk 
 to Rule Them All exercise challenge with submission of a completed 
 tracker.\n\n \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness, One Walk
