SUMMARY:Is this AI? Spotting Misinformation Online
DESCRIPTION:It is almost impossible to be online today without encountering 
 content generated by artificial intelligence (AI). Whether you are looking 
 for the latest news\, scrolling through posts on social media\, or looking 
 up a new recipe for dinner\, AI has made it more difficult to tell if what 
 we see online can be trusted. \n\nThis presentation will cover some of the 
 clues we can look for to determine if something has been generated by AI 
 and help you learn skills to verify the information you find online.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Digital/Tech Literacy
