SUMMARY:Songs We Carry: Exploring Music\, Memory\, and Family Stories
DESCRIPTION:What songs carry memories of the people and places that have 
 shaped us? In this interactive workshop\, participants will reflect on 
 songs connected to family\, home\, heritage\, or tradition and create a 
 small collage-style memento that brings together music\, memory\, images\, 
 and words. Together\, we’ll explore the ways songs can hold stories\, 
 connect generations\, and become part of the everyday archives we carry 
 with us.\n\nLed by Duke music professor Dr. Sophia Enriquez\, part of 
 “Forum @ the Library”  - a monthly series featuring Duke faculty 
 sharing their work in an interactive format\, hosted by the Library in 
 partnership with Duke’s Forum for Scholars and Publics at the Franklin 
 Humanities Institute.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Larkin Coffey":MAILTO:lcoffey@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Music
