SUMMARY:Book Babies
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for special bonding time with your little one 
 (aged 0-24 months)! At this lapsit-style storytime\, we will spend about 20 
 minutes engaging in structured learning through bounces\, rhymes\, songs\, 
 and books\, followed by 15-45 minutes of unstructured play and 
 socialization time.\n\nNote: A television is used during the first part of 
 the program (about 20 minutes) to display the words to the songs and rhymes 
 (to support adult engagement)\; there are no moving pictures. \n\nThis 
 program will be held on September 11\, 2026\, at 9:45 a.m. at North 
 Regional Library. The address is 221 Milton Rd. Durham\, NC 27712.\n\nOpen 
 for all! If you have any accessibility questions or accommodation needs\, 
 please contact Chelsea at cromero@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests be 
 made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we can 
 provide the best accommodations possible! Thank you!
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Chelsea Romero":MAILTO:cromero@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-16508949
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/16508949
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20260911T140000Z
DTEND:20260911T150000Z
DTSTAMP:20260911T000000Z
SUMMARY:Memory Cafe
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a monthly activity for people with dementia 
 and their caregivers. Memory Cafes host activities designed to engage in 
 the present\, without the expectations of using short-term memory or 
 forward thinking. This month\, we will be celebrating Grandparent's Day 
 with a special intergenerational story time! We'll join Book Babies to read 
 stories\, sing songs\, and visit with other families. Feel free to invite 
 your family members to join us for this special Memory Cafe.   \n\nThis 
 program will be held on September 11\, 2026\, at 10 a.m. at the North 
 Regional Library on the patio near the Children's Unit. The address is 221 
 Milton Rd.\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact me at dpeterson@dconc.gov. We ask that all requests 
 be made at least three (3) business days prior to the event to ensure we 
 can provide the best accommodations possible! Please email me if you plan 
 to attend and have nut allergies so that we can make accommodations.
LOCATION:North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Desiree Peterson":MAILTO:dpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Low Sensory Stimulation, Summer Reading
